/*
  ColorConverter.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0013 · ColorConverter (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  ColorConverter resolves (table "ColorConverter") lives here with its web
  t(key, default) English value. These entries fold into the app
  Localizable.xcstrings master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without
  editing the shared catalog (parallel-unsafe across the concurrent slots).

  The first block is the exact set of keys extracted from the web source
  (features/admin/components/devtools/tools/ColorConverter.tsx). The web en.json
  has no entry for "Color Converter" / "Color Converter Desc" / "Hex Color", so
  i18next renders those keys as-is — the native fallbacks reproduce that exactly.
  The RGB/HSL/HEX card labels are literal (untranslated) in the web source, so
  they travel as data, not as i18n keys. The remaining keys back native-only
  chrome (the unparseable-input hint, the swatch accessibility label).
*/

/* --- Keys from the web source (parity) --- */
"Color Converter" = "Color Converter";
"Color Converter Desc" = "Color Converter Desc";
"Hex Color" = "Hex Color";

/* --- Native chrome: empty hint + swatch accessibility --- */
"Color Converter Empty Hint" = "Enter a 6-digit hex color (for example, #3b82f6) to see its RGB and HSL values.";
"Color Swatch" = "Color swatch";
